          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The phrase is a direct, solemn avowal of the speaker's present love. It answers Maria's question about whether his apparent change of heart is genuine rather than temporary regret or self-deception.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke noget, Du nu bilder Dig ind\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The focal expression avows love but does not itself specify an action, obligation, or promise being undertaken. The following statement about living and dying with Maria may carry separate commitment implications, but that force should not be transferred to the focal phrase.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is highly emotional, the focal phrase is presented as a deliberate answer and reasoned reassurance, not as a reflex-like or uncontrolled affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer:\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.88,\"reason\":\"Its responsive reassurance function is adequately explained by the strong truth-presenting avowal under T; no distinct residual core force is established.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Men da jeg siger Maria dette, græder hun, fordi hun forstaar, jeg taler sandt\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"During an emotional face-to-face reunion, Maria asks whether the speaker's apparent love is genuine, lasting, and not something he will regret the next day. He answers with the focal avowal as part of a longer declaration explaining what he loves about her.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal phrase itself does not clearly undertake an obligation. A separate neighbouring statement—“Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.”—presents a lifelong shared future and may imply relational commitment. Maria's tears and happiness show uptake of his speech principally as truthful; the passage does not separately record explicit acceptance of defined undertaking terms.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work from the supplied text alone.\",\"limitations\":\"The supplied passage strongly supports the represented sincerity of the avowal through the speaker's prior self-reflection and the narration that Maria understands him to be speaking truthfully. It does not, however, define formal relationship terms or provide an explicit promise-and-acceptance exchange.\"}"
